# The image this action ships is Linux, and the scripts inside it are run by
# /bin/sh. A clone made on Windows under the default `core.autocrlf=true`
# would check these out with CRLF, and `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` is not an
# interpreter — the container exits 127 with "no such file or directory",
# naming the interpreter that plainly does exist. Pin the working tree, not
# just the repository, to LF so the checkout itself cannot introduce it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures are compared byte-for-byte by the test suites (and the SVRL ones
# are captured real validator output). Exclude them from any normalization so
# a future change to the rules above cannot silently rewrite the evidence.
test/fixtures/**            -text
formatter/test/fixtures/**  -text
